{"arm": "default", "set": "benchmark", "test": "H5-allowed-fork", "n": 3, "text": "1.Qc1, the queen on d1 slides sideways to c1! 1...Ne2+ shoots forward from d4 to e2, checking the king on g1, and after the king dances, the knight on e2 snatches the queen on c1 (2...Nxc1). 1.Qxd4 instead would have seen White's queen on d1 snatch the knight on d4.", "sentences": 3, "fallback_sentences": 0, "calls": 3, "seconds": 0.507, "meta": {"commit": "a519c9307e06ce66162d8cafe4b09488899149bb", "dirty": false, "positions_sha256": "36f722fb226e992904505fc6c53b709b6b1b9c7d566b9d1f01956a7e9d3341a3", "config_sha256": "a5b39f19d1f47550aff340bcf2bb8f83fca556667e7d00692c19610fca52cc03", "board_lines_sha256": "7afc00bf282719db9f973ac9ee74f0c14dfa004b4ddc8df4b67d8127c0506ef3", "think": false, "num_ctx": 4096, "model": "scan64-bench-gemma4-e4b-q4ks:latest", "model_digest": "d6b577f31405977a6343b5bb1ab12122ff00b5c5cd99267e0112eedf85757a02", "ollama_version": "0.40.18", "size_vram": 3051733647}}
{"arm": "default", "set": "benchmark", "test": "H5-allowed-fork", "n": 4, "text": "1.Qc1, the queen dances sideways from d1 to c1! Black's knight hops from d4 to e2 with 1...Ne2+ and checks the king on g1; then the knight on e2 snatches the queen on c1 with 2...Nxc1. 1.Qxd4 instead would have had White's queen on d1 seize the knight on d4.", "sentences": 3, "fallback_sentences": 0, "calls": 4, "seconds": 0.638, "meta": {"commit": "a519c9307e06ce66162d8cafe4b09488899149bb", "dirty": false, "positions_sha256": "36f722fb226e992904505fc6c53b709b6b1b9c7d566b9d1f01956a7e9d3341a3", "config_sha256": "a5b39f19d1f47550aff340bcf2bb8f83fca556667e7d00692c19610fca52cc03", "board_lines_sha256": "7afc00bf282719db9f973ac9ee74f0c14dfa004b4ddc8df4b67d8127c0506ef3", "think": false, "num_ctx": 4096, "model": "scan64-bench-gemma4-e4b-q4ks:latest", "model_digest": "d6b577f31405977a6343b5bb1ab12122ff00b5c5cd99267e0112eedf85757a02", "ollama_version": "0.40.18", "size_vram": 3051733647}}
{"arm": "default", "set": "heldout", "test": "lasker_chess_strategy-28-2", "n": 0, "text": "1...c5 pushes the pawn from c7 to c5, and with that grand move, the queen on d8 finds her freedom! The bishop on f8 was already snug inside the pawn barricade of e7 and g7 before 1...c5, and 1...c5 does nothing to loosen its grip. 2.Nf3, the knight from g1 leaps forward to f3. Black could have marched its pawn from e7 to e5 with 1...e5, freeing the bishop on f8.", "sentences": 4, "fallback_sentences": 0, "calls": 6, "seconds": 0.942, "meta": {"commit": "a519c9307e06ce66162d8cafe4b09488899149bb", "dirty": false, "positions_sha256": "36f722fb226e992904505fc6c53b709b6b1b9c7d566b9d1f01956a7e9d3341a3", "config_sha256": "a5b39f19d1f47550aff340bcf2bb8f83fca556667e7d00692c19610fca52cc03", "board_lines_sha256": "7afc00bf282719db9f973ac9ee74f0c14dfa004b4ddc8df4b67d8127c0506ef3", "think": false, "num_ctx": 4096, "model": "scan64-bench-gemma4-e4b-q4ks:latest", "model_digest": "d6b577f31405977a6343b5bb1ab12122ff00b5c5cd99267e0112eedf85757a02", "ollama_version": "0.40.18", "size_vram": 3051733647}}
{"arm": "default", "set": "heldout", "test": "lasker_chess_strategy-28-4", "n": 0, "text": "The knight on g8 marches forth to f6 with 2...Nf6, and this grand move frees the rook on h8! The bishop on c8 was already packed in tight by the pawns on b7 and d7 before 2...Nf6, and 2...Nf6 doesn't grant it freedom. 3.e5, the pawn from e4 advances to e5, and that piece on e5 now eyes the knight on f6. 2...d6 instead would have seen Black's pawn on d7 go forward to d6, letting the bishop on c8 stretch its legs.", "sentences": 4, "fallback_sentences": 0, "calls": 5, "seconds": 1.067, "meta": {"commit": "a519c9307e06ce66162d8cafe4b09488899149bb", "dirty": false, "positions_sha256": "36f722fb226e992904505fc6c53b709b6b1b9c7d566b9d1f01956a7e9d3341a3", "config_sha256": "a5b39f19d1f47550aff340bcf2bb8f83fca556667e7d00692c19610fca52cc03", "board_lines_sha256": "7afc00bf282719db9f973ac9ee74f0c14dfa004b4ddc8df4b67d8127c0506ef3", "think": false, "num_ctx": 4096, "model": "scan64-bench-gemma4-e4b-q4ks:latest", "model_digest": "d6b577f31405977a6343b5bb1ab12122ff00b5c5cd99267e0112eedf85757a02", "ollama_version": "0.40.18", "size_vram": 3051733647}}
{"arm": "default", "set": "heldout", "test": "lasker_chess_strategy-28-4", "n": 0, "text": "2...Nf6, the knight from g8 marches to f6, and suddenly the rook on h8 is free to roam! Even before 2...Nf6, the bishop on c8 was trapped behind the pawns on b7 and d7, and 2...Nf6 doesn't grant it freedom. 3.e5. The pawn from e4 springs forth to e5, and now it aims a pointy spear at the knight on f6. 2...d6 instead of 2...Nf6 could have seen Black's pawn on d7 marching to d6, freeing the bishop on c8.", "sentences": 4, "fallback_sentences": 0, "calls": 5, "seconds": 0.99, "meta": {"commit": "a519c9307e06ce66162d8cafe4b09488899149bb", "dirty": false, "positions_sha256": "36f722fb226e992904505fc6c53b709b6b1b9c7d566b9d1f01956a7e9d3341a3", "config_sha256": "a5b39f19d1f47550aff340bcf2bb8f83fca556667e7d00692c19610fca52cc03", "board_lines_sha256": "7afc00bf282719db9f973ac9ee74f0c14dfa004b4ddc8df4b67d8127c0506ef3", "think": false, "num_ctx": 4096, "model": "scan64-bench-gemma4-e4b-q4ks:latest", "model_digest": "d6b577f31405977a6343b5bb1ab12122ff00b5c5cd99267e0112eedf85757a02", "ollama_version": "0.40.18", "size_vram": 3051733647}}
